Ragged Roost is an abandoned mining town a little under a day's drive out of [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]], barely on modern maps. Its mine was small, and once ore could be shipped in from the [[Phenomena/Infinite Horizon|Infinite Horizon]] for less than it cost to dig here, there was no reason to keep working it, so the Orgs took what was worth packing and left the rest. A rusted sign at the town line reads "Welcome to Ragged Roost, population"; the number was scribbled out to zero, and has since been written over again to 75,000. A main street runs through the town with a few streets branching off it, one and two story buildings, and above the town on the mountainside sits the old rock crusher and its conveyor, unused.

At the middle of town stands the completed Istrian strider, the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]], a platform carried on eight legs with buildings set on top, three or four stories up and the size of a cruise ship. It is larger than the town itself, so that Ragged Roost lies in its shadow, and its legs still carry scaffolding where the last materials are loaded aboard. The [[Phenomena/Pilgrimage|pilgrimage]] has dressed the main street with electric fairy lights on the old lamp posts and banners reading "Pilgrimage Welcome," and guests who hold [[Phenomena/Keystone|keystones]] pass through the town to be hoisted aboard in shipping crates beside one of the legs.

Crossing the town line brings a pins-and-needles feeling at the small of the back, and every raiment within the town turns a plain matte gray, all of them the same color, shape and size and half-transparent, so that no guest can be read for their god. The blessings themselves still work. [[Aut]]'s mark still shows on [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]] when he calls it up, and still answers him.

Beyond the main street, a path marked with crossed swords leads to a disused train yard where Harlequins run a trial by combat, and one marked with a fairy ring leads off toward the town's outskirts.
